# Rebuild: ELF rebuilt with bkpt 0xAB semihosting exit in bench_main.c:128-132 and low header 0x2000D000/0x2000E000 (64K QEMU compat, see bench.ld).
# Original intended command (from triangulate.ps1):
#   qemu-system-arm -M mps2-an385 -nographic -kernel tools/renode/out/bench-m3.elf -d instr -D tools/qemu/qemu.log -semihosting
# Actual working command (mps2-an385 faults at 0x08000000; netduino2/stm32vldiscovery map 0x08000000 correctly):
#   timeout 10 qemu-system-arm -M <board> -nographic -kernel out/bench-<core>.elf -semihosting -singlestep -d exec -D /tmp/qemu-<core>.log && wc -l /tmp/qemu-<core>.log
# QEMU system-mode has no -d instr (user-mode only); with -singlestep, -d exec logs one line per retired instruction (closest to instr count).
# Without -singlestep, -d exec logs one line per translation block (TB) — order-of-magnitude smaller.

