## Board mapping & limitation
# m0plus -> mps2-an385 per task (Cortex-M3, closest for M0+; QEMU has no M0 with 0x08000000 flash). mps2-an385 flash is 0x00000000, so bench.ld 0x08000000 faults (Lockup HardFault R15=0). Fallback netduino2 (M3, flash 0x08000000, 64K RAM).
# m3 -> mps2-an385 or netduino2 -> netduino2 (working)
# m4 -> netduino2 or mps2-an385 -> netduino2 (netduinoplus2 also M4, same 0x08000000)
# m33 -> mps2-an385 per task (M3) or mps2-an505 (true M33, flash 0x00000000, also faults at 0x08000000). Fallback netduino2 (M33 binary on M3 CPU, no DSP/FPU in this workload).
# Extra: stm32vldiscovery (M3, 0x08000000) also works: 5198821 vs netduino2 8039624 for same 8s (1.55x board timing diff, not core).

## Notes
# - Entry 0x080003fc (bench-m3 low-header) correctly maps on netduino2/stm32vldiscovery; mps2-an385/an386/an505 fault (Lockup HardFault) because flash base 0x00000000/0x01000000.
# - -M netduino2 is the working triangulation board for this ELF layout (FLASH 0x08000000, RAM 0x20000000). Microbit (M0) also faults (expected flash 0x00000000 mismatch).
# - Low header 0x2000D000/0x2000E000 (heap 0x20008000, stack 0x2000C000) fits QEMU 64K and Renode 256K; high 0x2003D000/0x2003E000 overflows QEMU RAM (stack/Header invalid writes, now fixed). Renode driver updated to 0x2000D00C.
# - bkpt #0xAB at bench_main.c:128 (movs r0,#0x18; ldr r1,=0x20026; bkpt) traps QEMU -semihosting (ADP_Stopped_ApplicationExit) and exits cleanly when bench completes (avoids startup.s b 5b idle spin). Bench full run >60s wall in singlestep, so timeout 10 still needed for window counts; longer or record-only bench would exit via bkpt before timeout.
# - Without -singlestep, TB counts 92-355 vs static 23k vs dynamic 2-7M — TB << instr. With -singlestep, exec lines ~5-7M in 10s (~0.5M instr/s wall), vs static 23k (code size) — dynamic >> static as expected (loop iterates).
# - For per-core Thumb-1 vs Thumb-2 code density, static proxy 1.50x (34653/23077) is the stable magnitude check; QEMU wall-window 0.84-2.11x is host-variant but same direction (more Thumb-1 instr ↔ slower). See triangulate.log for cross-core proxy and Renode 1.78-2.23x.
